{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"'];print(json.dumps(s['UnderstandingChange'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"impact\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"clarification\",\n        \"meaning\",\n        \"dependency\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Impact\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"preserves\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"Shared sourced explanation of why the existing propositions, premises and observations still apply\",\n      \"title\": \"Preserves\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"challenges\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Saved Candidate IDs and the concrete premise or interpretation challenged by this knowledge\",\n      \"title\": \"Challenges\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"impact\",\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"source_ids\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"UnderstandingChange\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > prepare_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'))\nq=r['candidates'][0]['question'].copy()\nq.update(disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',unknowns=['Whether a fixed check can exhibit a repeatable suffix with all behavior-determining protocol, storage, queue and scheduling state accounted for, rather than only bounded non-completion.'],trigger_rationale='The legal producer-history exploration completed: a committed implicit change overlapped transfer, one emitted TimeoutNow was lost, the transfer expired and all Ready/application/network work drained. A fresh fixed check should determine whether normal reliable tick/message processing forms a recurrent joint-state suffix. No numeric exit deadline is inferred; the repeatability argument must account for all enabled work. The no-transfer control and later client-proposal rescue explain the trigger but do not themselves prove the duty was violated.')\nq['source_ids']+=['s_auto_ownership','s_raw_state','s_log_state','s_progress_state','s_inflight_state','s_determinism']\nq['counterevidence']+=['Retained exploration e3c2ba7fe2ee42f0a688d757f326d034 exits without transfer and exits after a later ordinary proposal; the suspected failure is conditional on the absence of that extra stimulus.']\nclaim={'id':'claim_auto_joint_continuation','kind':'obligation','concern':'implementation_semantics','description':'After an implicit joint configuration has been committed and applied, Raft must retain an implementation-owned continuation that eventually initiates exit once doing so is possible. If a temporary leader transfer rejects the initial exit proposal and subsequently aborts, a continuing eligible leader with available joint quorums, regular ticks and completed storage/application work must not remain indefinitely in that joint configuration solely because no unrelated client proposal or explicit leave-joint request arrives.','source_ids':['s_joint_contract','s_conf_contract','s_auto_ownership','s_applied','s_proposal_read','s_ticks_roles','s_abort','s_apply_completion'], 'scope':{'description':'Implicit joint transitions under a stable current leader after a failed transfer, with caller transport, storage and application duties fulfilled. The obligation is automatic continuation, not a time bound on exit.','assumptions':['Crash-fault protocol participants; no Byzantine message fabrication or state mutation.','Reliable transport after a finite loss, continued regular ticks, quorums available in both configurations, no subsequent forced leadership change.','Caller persists Ready before sending messages, applies committed configurations in order, and completes each Ready with Advance (or obeys corresponding async completion duties).','No continuing leadership-transfer request, explicit configuration request or unrelated workload is required to rescue Raft-owned implicit exit.'],'excluded':['A particular numeric deadline for automatic exit.','Arbitrary proposal completion guarantees; explicit joint mode assigns exit to the application.','Client availability or consensus safety loss beyond the missing automatic configuration continuation.','Infinite leader churn, indefinitely unavailable quorum or storage/application failure.'],'parameters':{'transition':'ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit'}},'pending':[],'grounding':{'source_ids':['s_applied','s_proposal_read','s_ticks_roles','s_abort','s_apply_completion'],'expectation_ids':['s_joint_contract','s_conf_contract','s_auto_ownership'],'binding_ids':['bind_auto_exit','bind_transfer_abort'],'derivation':'raft.proto assigns implicit exit to Raft by proposing a zero change, and assigns explicit-mode exit to the application. tracker.Config states that AutoLeave means transition should be carried out automatically by Raft when possible. This establishes an implementation-owned continuation duty with no numerical deadline. The generic Node proposal retry contract concerns caller proposals; it does not transfer ownership of Raft-generated implicit exit to the caller. appliedTo documents transfer rejection and relies on later applied work. The question is whether that work is guaranteed or whether the implementation can become recurrent while exit remains possible.','applicability':'The initial implicit proposal must actually commit and be applied before this responsibility is owed. A transfer rejection alone is not a violation; the temporary blocker must clear under the stated availability/scheduling assumptions. A repeated no-exit execution cycle must cover all relevant state and enabled work before supporting indefinite loss.','unresolved':[],'conflicts':[],'alternatives':['A later applied entry or new leader supplies a valid retry; these do not establish automatic continuation for a stable idle leader after failed transfer.','Application could explicitly propose an exit, but that is the contrasting explicit-mode duty.']}}\nbindings=[]\nfor id,material,symbol,start,end,description in [('bind_auto_exit','s_applied','raft.appliedTo',740,766,'Tests completion index, AutoLeave and leader role, then routes the automatic exit proposal through ordinary Step.'),('bind_transfer_abort','s_abort','raft.abortLeaderTransfer',2057,2059,'Clears the proposal-admission blocker when leadership transfer is abandoned; this function schedules no retry.')]:\n bindings.append(dict(id=id,material_id=material,symbol=symbol,start_line=start,end_line=end,description=description,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=claim['source_ids'],rationale='The owned automatic-exit trigger and the clearing of its temporary admission blocker jointly implement the continuation duty.')]))\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='b_application':\n  b['important_branches']=['Automatic exit uses ordinary Step and can be rejected during transfer. appliedTo is retriggered by nonempty MsgStorageApplyResp or snapshot completion; Advance on an empty committed-entry batch does not synthesize such an event.']\n  b['unknowns']=[]\n if b['id']=='b_transfer':\n  b['important_branches']=['Drops proposals while transfer active.','At election timeout a continuing leader clears leadTransferee; abortLeaderTransfer does not propose or schedule configuration work. A successful new leader separately appends an empty entry through role transition.']\n  b['unknowns']=[]\nm['core_overview']['open_details'][0]='Whether the source-local absence of an automatic-exit retry after transfer abort admits a complete recurrent execution suffix under continued caller service.'\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']=m['core_overview']['connection']['explanation'].replace('Applying a joint configuration sets AutoLeave; application completion may propose its exit, while concurrent transfer may reject that proposal.','Applying a joint configuration sets AutoLeave; application completion may propose its exit, while concurrent transfer may reject that proposal. Transfer abort only clears the admission blocker. Another nonempty application completion or snapshot completion can retry; an empty Ready/Advance does not itself invoke appliedTo.')\nchanges={}\nfor id in ['b_application','b_transfer','core_overview']:\n changes[id]={'impact':'clarification','source_ids':['s_applied','s_dispatch','s_apply_completion','s_ticks_roles','s_abort'],'rationale':'Trace completion producers and distinguish clearing transfer state from scheduling a subsequent automatic proposal. Removes answered source-level trigger unknowns, while the Candidate retains the execution-cycle discriminator.','preserves':'The principal Fact still asserts active joint configuration and assigned AutoLeave ownership, not successful scheduling. The selected Candidate already concerns rejection followed by failed transfer; its independent repeatability premise remains open.'}\njson.dump(m,open('continuation-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nfeedback={'ref_ids':['584b72abffa84bc88a7de31800f4271d','e3c2ba7fe2ee42f0a688d757f326d034','b_application','b_transfer','s_applied','s_abort','s_apply_completion','s_auto_ownership'],'answered':'Exploration e3c2ba7fe2ee42f0a688d757f326d034 produced an actual three-node term-2 election and implicit removal of node 3 at index 3. Transfer to caught-up node 2 began before leader configuration application; exactly one emitted MsgTimeoutNow was dropped. All nodes applied index 3. At 10 ticks transfer was cleared, and through 40 ticks the leader remained joint with AutoLeave=true, applied=commit=last=3; network queues, unstable entries, messages and stepsOnAdvance were empty and HasReady=false. A subsequent ordinary proposal committed at index 4 and automatic exit at index 5. The no-transfer control automatically exited at index 4. These are exploration observations, not formal property Evidence. Source search finds normal appliedTo calls only from nonempty application completion and snapshot completion; transfer abort and empty Advance do not supply them.','remaining':['The finite observations exclude undrained Ready/application work in this history, but do not alone establish indefinite stalling. A separately fixed check must account for full protocol/storage/scheduling state and a recurrent suffix.','The result does not show global inability to commit ordinary work; the diagnostic proposal demonstrates the opposite.'], 'understanding':'updated','rationale':'The actual producer history and scoped continuation contract justify constructing a fixed check. Keep the successful control and rescue as counterevidence; do not turn a tick count into an invented deadline.'}\np=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=r['candidates'][0]['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,rationale='Ground the implicit-exit continuation duty separately from its proposed recurrent-suffix evidence. The legal overlap and bounded observations are retained as exploration knowledge.',feedback=feedback,map_path='continuation-map.json',map_changes=changes,sources=[dict(id='s_raw_state',file='raft.go',start_line=341,end_line=435,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s_log_state',file='log.go',start_line=24,end_line=63,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s_progress_state',file='tracker/progress.go',start_line=25,end_line=115,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s_inflight_state',file='tracker/inflights.go',start_line=17,end_line=42,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s_determinism',file='README.md',start_line=10,end_line=14,kind='document_statement')])\njson.dump(p,open('obligation-submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python prepare_obligation.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_17-36-49-etcd_raft-real-run --submission obligation-submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
